{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/246862-wolf-s-children","id":246862,"title":"Wolf's Children","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-02T09:54:10-07:00","id":246862,"title":"Wolf's Children","content":"Saw anime on topic of children from werewolf father and his family. Got to thinking how will new family relations will work in 2e of <b>Forsaken</b>, with removal of Unhir. What do you think on this?<br /> <br /> Is it will look like this? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/8xLji7WsW0w\" data-code=\"8xLji7WsW0w\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/8xLji7WsW0w/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T11:49:27-07:00","id":247009,"title":"","content":"1)<i>Omigod I love this movie</i>.<br /> <br /> Like, you have no idea. I arranged a crowdfunding to get it to show here, and paid a big chunk of my own money to boot.<br /> <br /> 2)It's a note, but it's not the werewolf father who raises them, but the completely human mother who raises two kids who, from birth, can live as humans and wolves.<br /> <br /> I don't mean to imply it's light, but it is a more lighthearted look into that sort of thing for Forsaken. Still, they have a lot of neat moments that tie into the fearful moments of both werewolves and their families, and the emotion of dealing with those sorts of things, and I'm not just talking about Rage filled moments, as well as the struggle with a werewolf's sense of place in the world. It just as well shows the joys of a pack and of being a human and a wolf, and even with simply enjoying the world.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I'd recommend it. It hits a certain side of Forsaken,and is more pertinent than might be apparent.<br /> <br /> EDIT: All that said, no, I don't think that family is what a Forsaken family would look like all the time. It's a bit more...complicated in the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-02-2014, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T11:53:22-07:00","id":247012,"title":"","content":"Depends on how early first change is. Really the film is more about a single mother raising children to make rough choices in life based on their income and societal problems. It's a fantastic werewolf movie but I dunno if it would convey 2nd ed werewolf raising. Probably more like 1ed with one very on the ball werewolf parent, but this time both gaurd the nest. Or actually the chroniclers guide has a setting back for first edition about breeding, I may just go read that now...<br /> <br /> Wolf children ame and yuki is an amazing movie though. A touch depressing but still good. The manga adds a bit more to it as when (spoilers for first 20 minutes) happens, if gives Hannah dialogue that she doesn't have in the anime. The silent works better for visual effect, but it's a bit more crushing when you know what she's saying to him. <br /> <br /> Kinda like in the last of us when Joel saves Ellie from pedo cannibal, and it's just silence acoustic guitar as he comforts her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T15:55:05-07:00","id":247212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/246862-wolf-s-children?p=247009#post247009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1)<i>Omigod I love this movie</i>.<br /> <br /> Like, you have no idea. I arranged a crowdfunding to get it to show here, and paid a big chunk of my own money to boot.<br /> <br /> 2)It's a note, but it's not the werewolf father who raises them, but the completely human mother who raises two kids who, from birth, can live as humans and wolves.<br /> <br /> I don't mean to imply it's light, but it is a more lighthearted look into that sort of thing for Forsaken. Still, they have a lot of neat moments that tie into the fearful moments of both werewolves and their families, and the emotion of dealing with those sorts of things, and I'm not just talking about Rage filled moments, as well as the struggle with a werewolf's sense of place in the world. It just as well shows the joys of a pack and of being a human and a wolf, and even with simply enjoying the world.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I'd recommend it. It hits a certain side of Forsaken,and is more pertinent than might be apparent.<br /> <br /> EDIT: All that said, no, I don't think that family is what a Forsaken family would look like all the time. It's a bit more...complicated in the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>For starters? No Lunacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T15:59:22-07:00","id":247216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/246862-wolf-s-children?p=247212#post247212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For starters? No Lunacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a hundred percent sure that Lunacy affects those who'd be in a pack, but without additional information, very much yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T00:11:34-07:00","id":247553,"title":"","content":"But how this &quot;No Lunacy in Pack&quot; would look like?<br /> <br /> - Uratha to his beloved human:&quot;I'm loving you.&quot;<br /> - Lover:&quot;I love you too.&quot;<br /> - Uratha:&quot;So I must say you I'm... &lt;change in to Urshul&gt; THIS.&quot;<br /> -Lover:&quot;Oh, I love you so much, I'm not fearing you with ancient curse of madness now&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hmm? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"